    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office opened in 1870, marking the first permanent federal presence in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Mills%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Stampfli Ranch stretched from Main Street up the mountainside and into the flat Indian Valley beyond.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Mills%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mary A. Stampfli’s 1867 burial on the ranch created the family cemetery that still lies on the property today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Mills%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Indian Valley, a wide flatland east of the ranch, was the original settlement area for the Stampfli family and later other pioneers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
